          "title": "You'll want to know: تأبين",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تأبين — taʾbīn — \"a eulogy, a memorial tribute\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "حضر الكتاب حفل تأبين الشاعر. ḥaḍara al-kuttāb ḥafl taʾbīn ash-shāʿir. The writers attended the poet’s memorial."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تأبين (taʾbīn) is built on the native Arabic root ʾ-b-n (Lane), where Form II abbana is \"to praise a person after his death\"; taʾbīn is its verbal noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
